From b968893b7d1215f5fc0ee4eb113e0d2e2db95ace Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HelaFaye <dilsha21@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:23:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] SPI displays (MIPI DCS), XPT2046 touch, SD cards over SPI

mipi-dbi-panel: ILI9341, ILI9488, ST7735, ST7789, ST7796 and GC9A01 on
an SSI bus, with D/C, reset and backlight lines. Frame memory,
CASET/RASET windows, MADCTL (MV/MX/MY/BGR), 12/16/18-bit pixels,
sleep, display on/off, inversion, idle, and the read commands drivers
probe with (RDDID, RDID1-4, RDDST, RDDPM, ...). Each panel is a graphic
console showing what the glass would (module mounting, BGR and IPS
inversion as properties), so screendump checks what firmware drew.

xpt2046: the resistive touch controller (also ADS7843/7846), 8 and 12
bit conversions, overlapped control bytes as drivers send them,
PENIRQ; touches from the pointer or qom-set x/y/pressed.

ssi-sd: user-creatable (pin-link wires its CS) with drive= to put a
card in the slot. The ESP32 and ESP32-S3 machines select all three.
